Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the function's address in the manifest the HAL writes for a chora: it names any function, and the chora could claim any device it was told.  Each chora is given the capability for the function beside its own, and stops.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: @[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: WRONG -- a capability for function [0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7], which is not its own

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_modules.c b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_modules.c
index 70316da0..29cc5870 100644
